      "sourceTextSha256": "1173a02c44efe56ff45523c0bcc3ab3a18650fe4ea1345ee83705c07c0e73509",
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel, then transfer to the port. On the floating Uros Islands, you will learn how local communities use totora reeds to build their islands, homes and boats. The archipelago has more than 40 man-made islands. You can shop for souvenirs and take a ride in a traditional reed boat.\n\nContinue to Taquile, where residents keep traditional hand-weaving techniques alive. In 2005, UNESCO recognised the island’s textile art as a Masterpiece of the Oral and Intangible Heritage of Humanity. Have lunch on the island and return to Puno after the tour. Overnight at the 4-star Casona Plaza or a similar hotel as specified in the itinerary. Accommodation for the 3-star package is confirmed against the rate table.",
